Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.789 --> 00:00:05.190
Hey David, can you explain what dog whistles
are in politics?

00:00:05.190 --> 00:00:06.190
This is a good question.

00:00:06.190 --> 00:00:07.970
We talk about dog whistles all the time.

00:00:07.970 --> 00:00:13.640
Oh, with Trump, we've talked about America
first and nationalism and all these different

00:00:13.640 --> 00:00:15.670
things as being dog whistles.

00:00:15.670 --> 00:00:16.900
What do we mean by that though?

00:00:16.900 --> 00:00:24.240
So dog whistles are coded language that sounds
completely innocuous to some, usually to the

00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:29.830
larger public, but it has another meaning
for people who know what they're listening

00:00:29.830 --> 00:00:30.830
to.

00:00:30.830 --> 00:00:35.000
So it's called the dog whistle because there
is a such thing as a dog whistle when you

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:36.110
blow it.

00:00:36.110 --> 00:00:42.540
I think if a house to a human ear, it sounds
just like a very low tone, unremarkable sound,

00:00:42.540 --> 00:00:43.640
if you can even hear it.

00:00:43.640 --> 00:00:45.310
It's been awhile since I've been around a
dog whistle.

00:00:45.310 --> 00:00:50.660
You basically just hear the air coming through
the whistle, but to a dog's hearing it lets

00:00:50.660 --> 00:00:52.900
them hear a noise that is, I think, high pitched.

00:00:52.900 --> 00:00:53.900
It riles them up.

00:00:53.900 --> 00:00:54.900
They hear it immediately.

00:00:54.900 --> 00:00:57.280
They think they're being called or whatever
the case may be.

00:00:57.280 --> 00:00:59.490
There are racist dog whistles.

00:00:59.490 --> 00:01:04.170
There are antisemitic dog whistles, there
are religious dog whistles.

00:01:04.170 --> 00:01:11.680
So here's some examples, inner city and urban
to refer to black people to those in the know

00:01:11.680 --> 00:01:13.729
with seemingly innocuous language.

00:01:13.729 --> 00:01:18.950
So we've heard, I've even interviewed some
people, Ben Shapiro use this term when I interviewed

00:01:18.950 --> 00:01:21.100
him about gun safety.

00:01:21.100 --> 00:01:27.740
We will hear, talk about to really deal with
gun violence, we need to focus on urban youth,

00:01:27.740 --> 00:01:30.540
inner city, whatever they're talking about
black people.

00:01:30.540 --> 00:01:33.840
It's about, we don't want black people having
guns, but white people having guns is fine.

00:01:33.840 --> 00:01:38.620
That is a dog whistle that sounds innocuous
from the language, but if you know what is

00:01:38.620 --> 00:01:40.520
meant, you understand it.

00:01:40.520 --> 00:01:45.970
Law and order, law and order, it sounds, I
mean listen, we have laws and we need order.

00:01:45.970 --> 00:01:48.010
We things that we need things to be in order.

00:01:48.010 --> 00:01:53.570
It has been used to signal anti-immigrant
ideas, racist ideas.

00:01:53.570 --> 00:01:58.180
It's been used as a signal by politicians
to say, don't worry, I'm for law and order

00:01:58.180 --> 00:02:05.010
coded to mean I'm not going to let immigrants
or black people get too much clout or status

00:02:05.010 --> 00:02:06.390
in society.

00:02:06.390 --> 00:02:10.759
Tough on crime is a similar one also that
is often connected to, it's just straight

00:02:10.759 --> 00:02:13.629
up racist policies like for example and frisk.

00:02:13.629 --> 00:02:17.469
Here's another example, Barack Hussein Obama.

00:02:17.469 --> 00:02:20.190
Now you might say that's the guys name.

00:02:20.190 --> 00:02:28.859
How could that be a dog whistle, but the people
